Building a foundation is a universal concept, from building one in the gospel so that you’re not shaken when the storms and winds come, to building one in real structures and concepts such as Kubernetes. 
When your foundation is solid, you can extrapolate and build amazing structures above it—structures that are solid and built upon a firm foundation.

In the gospel, when you build upon the rock of Jesus Christ, you can trust that when the storms and trials of life come, you will be able to endure with Him. Nothing that comes your way can shake you, and even if you stumble, 
you have a foundation to rely upon.

I think that with the foundations of concepts, we can understand and really dive deeply into what’s happening. From those small and basic understandings comes a great ability to build amazing things.
Oftentimes, the small and simple things can be used to accomplish great things.

If you’re willing to work on your foundation and build up your basic skills and knowledge,
you can be assured that the rest will come much more easily.
